INT. GRAIN ELEVATOR CONTROL ROOM - NIGHT

A glass booth bolted to the side of a concrete silo. Dust on every surface. Gauges tick. A wall of dead monitors, one live.

TOMASZ KOWALCZYK (50s, shift supervisor, cardigan over a hi-vis vest) pours coffee into four mugs. Doesn't spill a drop.

ODALYS REYES-MBEKI (30s, auditor, grey blazer, laptop bag still on her shoulder) watches the pour.

BRANKA ILIĆ (40s, maintenance, oil-stained thumbs) sits on an overturned bucket, eating sunflower seeds.

PETROS ANAGNOS (20s, scale operator, headphones around his neck) stares at the live monitor.

WILLEM (teen, intern, too-big boots) stands by the door like he's waiting to be sent home.

TOMASZ
Milk's off. Sorry.

ODALYS
I don't take milk.

BRANKA
She doesn't take anything.

TOMASZ
Everybody takes something.

Odalys sets down her bag. Sits. Opens the laptop. The fan whirs loud in the quiet.

PETROS
Truck four's late.

BRANKA
Truck four's always late.

ODALYS
Truck four logged two loads Tuesday. The scale shows one.

Nobody moves. Branka cracks a seed. Spits the husk into her palm.

TOMASZ
Scale drifts.

PETROS
It doesn't drift. I calibrate it.

BRANKA
Every Friday.

PETROS
Every Friday.

ODALYS
Then it's eleven tons of wheat that went somewhere.

TOMASZ
Eleven. Is that the number?

ODALYS
Eleven point four.

Tomasz slides a mug toward her. She doesn't touch it. He slides one toward Willem too. Willem takes it with both hands.

WILLEM
Thanks, Mr. Kowalczyk.

TOMASZ
Tomasz.

BRANKA
Don't encourage him.

PETROS
(to Odalys)
You looked at the weighbridge camera?

ODALYS
It's been offline since March.

BRANKA
Since February.

TOMASZ
March.

BRANKA
February. I filed the ticket.

TOMASZ
You filed it in March.

Branka shrugs. Another seed. Petros pulls his headphones up over one ear, then lets them drop again.

ODALYS
Somebody wants to say something?

Silence. Outside, a conveyor belt shifts and groans. The mugs steam.

WILLEM
Truck four's here.

Headlights sweep across the glass. Everyone turns. Nobody stands.

TOMASZ
Let him wait.

PETROS
He'll honk.

BRANKA
He won't.

A long beat. No honk.

ODALYS
That's what I thought.

She types something. Tomasz drinks his coffee. His hand is perfectly steady.

TOMASZ
You drove four hours for this?

ODALYS
Five. Traffic.

BRANKA
Petros, show her the book.

PETROS
What book?

BRANKA
The paper book.

PETROS
(too fast)
There isn't a book.

Branka looks at him. Cracks a seed. Looks at Tomasz.

TOMASZ
There's a book.

Petros opens a drawer. Takes out a battered green ledger. Doesn't hand it over. Holds it flat on his knees.

ODALYS
I'll need that.

TOMASZ
In the morning.

ODALYS
Now.

TOMASZ
The morning, Ms. Reyes-Mbeki. Coffee first. Sleep. Then the book.

Odalys closes the laptop halfway. Studies each face in turn. Willem looks at the floor. Branka looks at the ceiling. Petros looks at the ledger.

Tomasz smiles, mild as milk that isn't off.

ODALYS
Fine.

She picks up the mug. Drinks. Makes a small face.

ODALYS (CONT'D)
It's cold.

TOMASZ
It was hot when I poured it.

Outside, the headlights go out.

FADE OUT.
